{
 "title": "Unsupervised Clustering of Multi-Instrument Psychometric Data: An Evaluation of Training Approaches",
 "pipeline": {
  "primary": "UMAP to 10 dimensions (n_neighbors=30, min_dist=0.0, euclidean, seed 42), then a variational Bayesian Gaussian Mixture with a Dirichlet-process prior (weight_concentration_prior=0.01, full covariance, k-means init, n_init=3, max_iter=300, reg_covar=1e-4). Components below 0.02 posterior weight are pruned; the survivors are the effective cluster count.",
  "robustness": "The same normalized trait matrix clustered without embedding by K-means, Ward linkage, and Gaussian mixtures with full and diagonal covariance, each at k = 2 to 5.",
